__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
# Virtual environments
.env
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
qiskit_hw/
.vscode/
*.pdf
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.dat
*.png
*.jpg
*.egg-info/
results/meetings/
results/hpc_run/
results_hpc_copy/
# The sweep and study directories are NOT excluded wholesale. They were until
# 2026-08-20, which kept every recorded number out of the repository: a reader
# checking a figure had no way to reach the archive it was drawn from. What is
# excluded instead is the BULK, by kind, in the rules further down --- the
# per-solution `.npz` fields (182 MB), the cluster logs (162 MB) and the
# diagnostic figure sets (48 MB). The summaries, tables and tidy figure datasets
# that remain come to about 7 MB, and are the provenance of every number quoted
# in the dissertation.
#
# Excluding by kind rather than by directory is deliberate and not
# interchangeable with it. Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a
# negation beneath one can never match --- which is exactly why the `docs/*`
# rule below has never tracked anything despite promising to. Any rule added
# here that names a directory forfeits the ability to keep anything inside it.
#
# The full set including the `.npz` fields belongs in a data deposit; see
# results/README.md.
!results/**/*.csv
updated*
CLAUDE.md
.agents
.claude
context/
# Documentation prose is tracked; generated artefacts under docs/ are not.
# The directory itself must stay un-excluded, otherwise git will not descend
# into it and the negation below can never match.
# Internal artefacts and temporary workspace files are excluded by default.
docs/*

# Ad hoc backup copies made before a cleanup or a rerun. One such directory was
# named "results.backup." with a TRAILING DOT, which Windows cannot create: once
# committed, no Windows clone could check the branch out at all, and git aborted
# with "invalid path" before any merge or rebase could begin. Excluded by pattern
# so that a hand-made backup can never be committed again.
results.backup*/
results_backup*/
*.backup/
*.bak
*.tar.gz

# The rules above match a backup FILE ("*.bak") and a directory whose name ends
# exactly in ".backup", but not the dated convention actually used before a
# re-run -- results/2Dstudies.bak_20260819 -- whose name ends in the date. Such a
# directory holds .json and .csv, neither excluded by kind below, so it surfaced
# as untracked content and the preflight refused the tree: a backup taken to make
# a submission safe was what stopped the submission. Match the name wherever it
# occurs and however it is suffixed.
*.bak*/
*_backup*/

# Generated cluster output, excluded by kind rather than by directory name.
# The per-directory rules above only protect the six sweep directories that
# exist today; a job writing to a new directory (a wave, a resumed sweep, a
# fresh order) would otherwise commit its solution archives and logs. The QSVT
# phase cache is the sole deliberate exception: those archives are the expensive
# precompute and are tracked on purpose.
*.npz
!results/qsvt_phase_cache/*.npz
*.log
*.err
*.out